<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="95f3b6dd-24de-532d-b46e-f3051da4d4b0" activityNameId="287c9b9e-d0a4-5003-97f0-7c0e4c2d4a5c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Cable, connector for computer, without plugs, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Cable, connector for computer, without plugs, at plant
This dataset can be applied to describe the production of a typical power cord/connector for computers. The total weight of 1 m of connector is 0.065 kg (without the belonging plugs). The information for this dataset is based on weighing, measurements and analysis at EMPA Laboratories. In 2023, only production efforts data are updated. Furthermore, material and energy input are now represented by global inventory flows; UUID: 48a49a0d-4ca9-3a63-9f6a-f48247e1a5c1
Describes the production of a typical electric cable (connector) for a desktop computer. Calculated per 1 m of connector. Included are the materials copper, TPE (elastomere) and PVC with their respective manufacturing processes. The infrastructure is calculated via the proxy "electronic component production plant". Further inventoried are the electricity for the assembly of the connector, the fuel oil, propane and water input, the disposal of plastic and rubber parts, the VOC and methanol emissions created during the processing, plus the road and rail transportation for input materials from the regional storage to the production site. The accumulated hazardous waste is also reported.
Location: The data describes a typical computer cable in 2006. The kind of cable is produced by international manufacturers and available all over the world. Therefore a global dataset is justifiable.
Technology: The manufacturing process is inventoried through wire drawing and extrusion of insulation and jacket (TPE, PVC) around wire.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Weighing and measuring of materials. Literature for electricity consumption (assembly), emissions and waste.
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: see Geography and Technology
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_48a49a0d-4ca9-3a63-9f6a-f48247e1a5c1.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
